\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan ends down vs dollar on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan closed down slightly against the U.S. dollar on Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a fairly active seller for the second consecutive day after the yuan reached 30-month closing high and breached the key 8.2800 level on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the yuan back to the 8.2800 level," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2800 to one dollar against 8.2798 on Thursday. Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2800, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2800 and advanced to an intraday high of 8.2760 with buyers trying to push it further up from the 8.2800 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to the 8.2800 level. The yuan touched a low of 8.2838. \par \par \uc2  "The selling shows buyers face opposition from the market's largest trader if they try to push the yuan up further," a second trader said. "This will dampen bullish sentiment in the short term." \par \par \uc2  The yuan had maintained its upward trend over the past few trading days on expectations it would be buoyed by year-end demand and a healthy trade surplus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to rise but only slightly early next week. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Friday closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.4850 to 100 yen from 6.5101. \par \par \uc2  It ended higher against the Hong Kong dollar at a day's low of 1.0710 to one dollar from 1.0720. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbs01wo4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
