\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends At New 3-Yr High Vs Dlr As Inflows Stay High \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1997\par 07:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (AP-Dow Jones)--The yuan ended narrowly higher against the U.S. dollar Monday, as dollar inflows outstripped outflows for another session, leaving the yuan at a new three-year high and straddling a key barrier, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading Center, the dollar closed at 8.2800 yuan, down from Friday's 8.2802 yuan. \par \par \uc2  After slipping through the key 8.2800-yuan barrier, the dollar gained slightly at the end of trade, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to slow the yuan's ascent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they widely expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is eager to avoid the negative effects a stronger yuan would have on China's state-run exporters. They added, however, they expect the yuan to break through the key 8.2800 point in coming sessions, as \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows stay high. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  requires the bulk of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  entering the country be converted into yuan. That puts significant pressure on the semi-convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise given China's hefty trade surplus and foreign direct investment. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the Hong Kong dollar closed at 1.0755 yuan, up from Friday's close of 1.0716, while the yen ended at 6.5475 yuan per 100 yen, down from the previous close of 6.5701. \par \par \uc2  In the non-deliverable forward market, which gives an indication of how participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in the coming few months, money broker Exco Group in Singapore on Monday was quoting the U.S. dollar at 8.9302 yuan for delivery in six months and at 9.2802 yuan over a one-year timeframe. \par \par \uc2  As the yuan is only convertible under the current account, trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is driven by commercial demand and not speculation, which is prohibited. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also enforces narrow trading margins for the yuan, both with official price limits for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a strong trading presence stabilizing even slight fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  -By Karby Leggett; 86 21 6279-7294; kleggett@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0647GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbo0906z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
