\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends little changed vs dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the dollar in Shanghai on Tuesday in dull trading, with the market taking a breather after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2807 to one dollar on Tuesday from 8.2809 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said as the yuan moved in a narrow range between 8.2802 and 8.2802, the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has no necessity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains last week were linked partly to expectations of a bigger trade surplus for the January-October period. Those expectations were borne out as the surplus in October was reported at $5.0 billion, giving a total surplus of $35.59 billion for the 10 months. \par \par \uc2  "With the trade data factored into the market last week, the yuan has no more positive factors to support further gains," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  "It has to wait for new stimulus to breach the key resistance level of 8.2800," he said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at about the 8.2805 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said they expected the yuan to consolidate below the 8.2800 level on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The 8.2800 level is an important resistance level. If that level is breached, the market will see intensified pressure for an appreciation," a dealer said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is certain to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yuan below that level in the near future." \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2805. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.5755 to 100 yen from 6.6518. It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday high of 1.0712 to one dollar from 1.0729. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbi02cg6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
