\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up at 29-month high vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 3 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan ended up at a 29-month closing high against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Monday due to active buying late in the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday high of 8.2810 to one dollar on Monday against 8.2828 on Friday. It was the strongest close since May 17, 1995 when the yuan ended at 8.2805. \par \par \uc2  It was also the second consecutive trading day that the yuan has hit a 29-month closing high, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than last Friday with most business done around the 8.2828 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan moved in a broad range for most of the session on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But strong buying emerged in late trading as investors took heart that favourable economic data and healthy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves would continue to lend support to the yuan, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said further gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had in the past repeatedly acted to prevent the yuan from rising too sharply. \par \par \uc2  They said they expected the yuan to fall due to a correction on Tuesday following sharp gains. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at 8.2828 on Monday and moved in a range of 8.2820 and 8.2840 for most of the session, hitting an intraday low of 8.2904. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2834. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down slightly against Japanese yen at 6.8830 to 100 yen from 6.8718. \par \par \uc2  It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday high of 1.0691 to one dollar from 1.0724. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb303ec8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
