\par\par \b \uc2  As Speculators Target HK Dlr, China's Yuan Comes Into Focus \b0\par\par\uc2  By Karby Leggett \par \uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1997\par 10:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (AP-Dow Jones)--Could China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, be the next Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tumble? Quite likely, many economists and analysts say, though the reasons and timing for a mainland devaluation are a far stretch from those that have sunk regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent months. \par \par \uc2  No one is saying the yuan is in imminent danger. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is transacted under the current account only, or for trade in goods and services; speculators can't lay hands on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unless they have a trade-related reason. China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also keeps a close watch on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily to hold the yuan in a range it deems suitable for domestic state-owned manufacturers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, as Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  crumble, the yuan has been on a decidedly different course - strengthening. Massive net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows - most stemming from high levels of foreign investment - and slim outflows have kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under strong upward pressure for the last three years. \par \par \uc2  But now, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators turn their sights on Hong Kong, some are wondering aloud for the first time if the yuan - the last U.S.-dollar linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region after Hong Kong - will be able to weather the ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  storm. \par \par \uc2  Mounting competitive pressure from cheaper regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given rise to worries that China's growth in 1998 may be much slower than forecast. That's because mainland exports, a key component of China's economy, could suffer from the new competition with southeast Asia. \par \par \uc2  That could pressure PBoC to allow the yuan to weaken during the next 12 months, many economists say. Otherwise, it would risk an economic slump at a time when millions of Chinese workers are set to be thrown out of jobs as the government launches a sweeping restructuring of state-owned companies. \par \par \uc2  'At this point, if the Hong Kong dollar peg goes, then the only one left is the reminbi,' says a regional strategist at a large U.K. investment bank in Hong Kong. 'Sooner or later, China will have to depreciate...and its possible the PBoC may just decide to do it.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0939GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 55128 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtar0837h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
