\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends unchanged against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed unchanged at 8.2840 to the U.S. dollar in dull trading on Monday due to a prevailing wait-and-see attitude on the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Most business was done at 8.2836, the traders said. \par \par \uc2  Bank traders were sidelined after the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to check the yuan's strong upward trend, triggered by an oversupply of dollars that was mainly due to China's surging foreign trade surplus, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Bank traders took a cautious attitude on Monday due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  "This made the yuan move in a narrow range in dull activity on Monday," he said. \par \par \uc2  A second trader said the yuan still had potential to go up if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Bullish sentiment towards the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the oversupply of dollars will soon push the yuan to the 8.2830 level once the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Monday opened unchanged at 8.2840 and rose slightly to hit an intraday high of 8.2834 early in trading. It then consolidated down, hitting a low of 8.2841. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2839. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Monday closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.8250 to 100 yen from 6.8650. \par \par \uc2  It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday high of 1.0700 to one dollar from 1.0705. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtak041rq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
