\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends up against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 16 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed up against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Thursday on a technical correction after Beijing announced a sharp rise in its foreign trade surplus, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2842 to one dollar from 8.2878. Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2841, traders said. \par \par \uc2  China's foreign trade surplus surged to $30.57 billion in the first nine months of this year against $8.04 billion in the same period of 1996, state television said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The surge boosted buying interest on Thursday, helping to push up the yuan at the close," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's rebound came after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply on Wednesday due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the gain, traders said market sentiment was cautious after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yuan's upward trend on each of the previous three days. \par \par \uc2  "The market now pays more attention to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions," a second trader said. "This will exert a lot of psychological pressure on the yuan in the short term." \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected investors to take a wait-and-see attitude in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to move around the 8.2840 level on Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Thursday opened higher but at an intraday low of 8.2845 to one U.S. dollar and moved below 8.2840 for most of the session, hitting a high of 8.2838 late in trading. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Wednesday was 8.2839. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at 6.8610 to 100 yen from 6.8260 and little changed agaist the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0710 to one dollar from 1.0711. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtag045p3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
