\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan ends down sharply on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed down sharply against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Wednesday mainly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  This was the third successive day the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yuan's upward trend, the traders said. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also hurt by new rules taking effect on Wednesday allowing big Chinese foreign trade firms to retain some \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  cash, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday low of 8.2878 on Wednesday from Tuesday's 8.2834. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than Tuesday with most business done at about 8.2840, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the yuan in the last few minutes of trading, making it end sharply down," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  "The successive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows the bank is determined to prevent the yuan from rising sharply, and it has greatly hurt bullish sentiment for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  New \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules took effect on Wednesday allowing major Chinese trading firms to retain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cash equivalent to 15 percent of their foreign trade volumes of the previous year. \par \par \uc2  Formerly, local firms had to sell all their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appointed state banks and buy it back when they needed it. \par \par \uc2  The new rules reduce the amount of dollars appointed banks have to trade on the market and this was seen by traders as helping relieve upward pressure on the yuan in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "But as there limits on the dollars the firms can hold onto, the impact seems to be more psychological than real," a second trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected to see a technical rebound in the yuan on Thursday with the price moving mainly around 8.2840. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan opened slightly up at an intraday high of 8.2831 against one U.S. dollar and went down slowly for most of the session before it began to plunge in the last few minutes of trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Tuesday was 8.2832. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed slightly up against the Japanese yen at 6.8260 to 100 yen from 6.8320. It ended higher against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0711 to one dollar from 1.0715. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtaf04bsd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
