\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan ends little changed vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed almost unchanged against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Tuesday due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising sharply, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars to depress the yuan after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the 8.2830 level, they said. It was the second day in a row that the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  made buyers cautions, leading the yuan to close little changed today," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2834 to one dollar on Tuesday from Monday's 8.2836. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull on Tuesday with most business done at about 8.2832, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said buying in the yuan continued in early trade on market expectations that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue its upward trend based on \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong foreign trade positions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw buyers retreat late in the session and the yuan move narrowly around 8.2830, they said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yuan was likely to move around the 8.2830 level on Wednesday because the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent strong signals that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not want the yuan to rise quickly. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Tuesday opened higher at 8.2831 and moved around 8.2830 early in trading, hitting an intraday high of 8.2829. \par \par \uc2  It then fell slightly to hit a low of 8.2844 late in the session. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2831. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.8320 to 100 yen from 6.8800. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0715 to one dollar from 1.0701. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtae049rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
