\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan ends little changed vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 13 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Monday despite bullish sentiment for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan continued to rise in early trade on Monday after sharp gains last week but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session, capping its upward trend, the traders said. \par \par \uc2  "There were signs that the bank was selling the yuan for dollars to prevent it from rising sharply," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed Monday at 8.2836 to one dollar from 8.2835 last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than last Friday with most business done at 8.2833, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A second trader said buying continued on Monday, pushing the yuan above the 8.2830 level in early trade, due to expecations of further rises of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on China's surging foreign trade surplus and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  "The continued rise after last week's heavy gains triggered the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the consolidation, traders said bullish pro-yuan sentiment did not change much and the yuan was likely to move at a higher level of 8.2830 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Monday opened up at 8.2832 and moved in a range of 8.2830 and 8.2840 for nearly the whole session, hitting an intraday high of 8.2814 and a low of 8.2880. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2835. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at 6.8800 to 100 yen from 6.8374. It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0701 to one dollar from 1.0710. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dtad01d02\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
