\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends at new 28-month high vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 8 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan ended up at another 28-month closing high against the U.S. dollar, aided by heavy dollar sales by domestic banks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday high of 8.2830 to one dollar from Tuesday's 8.2844. The close was the highest since May 17, 1995 when the yuan ended at 8.2805. \par \par \uc2  "Some major Chinese banks seem to have ample dollars in their hands and they sold them in volume in particularly in late trade," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan's upward trend in the past few weeks also helped it strengthen on Wednesday," he added. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active with most business done at about 8.2840, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A second trader said a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan helped boost bullish sentiment towards the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "With the yuan standing at high levels for weeks now, there have been few signs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress it in the recent days," he said. \par \par \uc2  "This has helped boost sentiment on Wednesday," he said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the short-term outlook promised a continued upward trend though a technical pullback could be expected on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan is likely to test the 8.2800 resistance in the short term," the second trader said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at an intraday low of 8.2844 on Wednesday and moved in a range of 8.2840 and 8.2842 for most of the session. The weighted average rate on Tuesday was 8.2845. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up slightly against the Japanese yen at 6.7701 to 100 yen from 6.7836. It ended higher against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0704 to one dolalr from 1.0709. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta801ew2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
