\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan ends up vs dollar at 28-month high. \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 7 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan ended slightly up against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Tuesday to hit a new 28-month closing high for the second consecutive day due to bullish sentiment for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2844 to one dollar against 8.2845 on Monday, the highest close since May 17, 1995 when the yuan ended at 8.2805. \par \par \uc2  "Bank traders believed the yuan would continue an upward trend in the short term," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  "They built fresh positions on Tuesday despite Monday's sharp rise, pushing the yuan to end up again," he said. \par \par \uc2  The bullish sentiment was mainly based on China's surging foreign trade surplus and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2844, they said. \par \par \uc2  A second trader said some bank traders began to take to the sidelines on Tuesday, expecting the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yuan from rising sharply. \par \par \uc2  "Some bank traders expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan, because it has been at such high levels for weeks now," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move down slightly on Wednesday on consolidation. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened little changed at 8.2844 and moved in a narrow range of 8.2842 and an intraday low of 8.2845 for most of the session, hitting a high of 8.2822. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2845. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up slightly against the Japanese yen at 6.7836 to 100 yen from 6.7922. \par \par \uc2  It closed down against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday low of 1.0709 to one dollar from 1.0697. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta701ky4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
