\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends little changed vs dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 29 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the dollar on Monday as light \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling kept the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a narrow trading range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But trade was thin with few participants willing to take new positions ahead of the long National Day holiday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2852 to the dollar on Monday from last Friday's finish of 8.2851. Trading will take a break from Wednesday through Saturday with a resumption on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan from rising above the 8.2850 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although on a modest scale, helped keep the yuan in a narrow range," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders had little interest in pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in either direction and most business was purely for commercial needs, another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained bullish, due mainly to China's surging foreign trade surplus and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, dealers said. But they added the local unit would probably not advance much further before the holiday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected the yuan to move narrowly around the 8.2850 level on Tuesday, the last trading day before the holiday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Monday moved in a tight range of 8.2850 to 8.2855 for most of the session. It touched an intraday high of 8.2825 and a low of 8.2902. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2850. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at an intraday low of 6.8455 to 100 yen from 6.8350 on Friday. It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0703 to one dollar. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9t01xel\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
