\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up at 28-month high vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 22 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan ended up at a 28-month closing high against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Monday due to widespread market expectations that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had further room to appreciate, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The market was oversupplied with dollars mainly due to China's surging foreign trade surplus while the yuan was undervalued due to repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent it from rising sharply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This triggered expectations of a rise, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2860 on Monday from 8.2865 last Friday, the highest close since May 17, 1995, when it ended at 8.2805. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at about 8.2860. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan continued to rise today after hitting a 28-month closing high three times last week, indicating pro-yuan sentiment was very strong on the market," one dealer said. "Many bank traders expected the yuan to continue to rise." \par \par \uc2  A second dealer said there were signs the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan at about the 8.2860 level to prevent it from rising too sharply. \par \par \uc2  "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have no intention of depressing the yuan further," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move narrowly around the 8.2860 level on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan opened slightly higher at 8.2863 and hit an intraday low of 8.2864 early in trading. \par \par \uc2  It then moved narrowly around 8.2860 for most of the session, hitting a high of 8.2828. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2864. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Monday closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.7700 to 100 yen from 6.7930 and little changed against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0698 to one dollar from 1.0699. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9m023jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
