\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Lower Against Dlr On Technical Correction \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1997\par 09:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (AP-Dow Jones)--The yuan ended slightly lower against the dollar Wednesday, falling on a technical correction after several days of gains, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At the Shanghai-based the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading Center, the dollar ended Wednesday at 8.2877 yuan, off narrowly from Tuesday's close of 8.2872 yuan. \par \par \uc2  Traders cited technical factors for the fall in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also called the renminbi. They said several sessions of heavy dollar selling that pushed the yuan to a new year high set the stage for the narrow retreat. \par \par \uc2  But they ruled out a continued easing in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that China's large trade surplus and strong foreign capital inflows are creating strong pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate, despite efforts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect it. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is the largest player in the market, and often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan weak for fear that a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hurt the competitiveness of state manufacturers. \par \par \uc2  In other trade, the Japanese yen ended at 6.8421 yuan per Y100, off from 6.8579 yuan, while the Hong Kong dollar closed at 1.0692 yuan, down from Tuesday's finish of 1.0699 yuan. \par \par \uc2  In the non-deliverable forward market, which gives an indication of how participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in the coming few months, money broker Exco Group in Singapore on Wednesday was quoting the U.S. dollar at 8.4571 yuan for delivery in six months and at 8.5871 yuan over a one-year timeframe. \par \par \uc2  As the yuan is only convertible under the current account, trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is driven by commercial demand and not speculation, which is prohibited. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also enforces narrow trading margins for the yuan, both with official price limits for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a strong trading presence stabilizing even slight fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-09-97 \par \par \uc2  0706GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9h06x8f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
