\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  yuan ends down vs dollar on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 10 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed lower at 8.2900 to the dollar on Wednesday against Tuesday's 8.2883 under pressure from selling of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars to depress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  "The move aimed to dampen bullish sentiment towards the yuan ahead of the announcement of foreign trade data," he said. \par \par \uc2  China will announce its August trade data this week and the market expects a solid surplus to mean more dollars being sold for yuan, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  led to speculative selling late in the session, further depressing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Most business was done at 8.2888, they said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected the yuan to bounce back slightly on Thursday after Wednesday's loss. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly higher at 8.2881 and hit an intraday high of 8.2838. It then fell steadily, touching a low of 8.2984. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Tuesday was 8.2881. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended down against the Japanese yen at 6.9301 to 100 yen against 6.9105 and up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0693 to one dollar from 1.0694. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt9a002vx\par }\page {\