\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Vows Vigilance In HK Dollar Market - Reports \b0\par\par\uc2 154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 03:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will remain vigilant this week in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after selling of the Hong Kong dollar last week and as the territory returns from a holiday. \par \par \uc2  The South China Morning Post said HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam Chi-kwong spoke at a 'hastily called press conference' on Monday, while Hong Kong markets were closed for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  Yam said there had been speculation against the Hong Kong dollar on Thursday and Friday last week, but that the activity lacked intensity. 'This situation is actually very stable and I feel comfortable about it,' said Yam, according to the Hong Kong Standard. The Post said he wouldn't comment about whether the authority \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  According to the South \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Morning Post, Yam said speculators had been defeated. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0101GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8j062ns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
