\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends up as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  eases  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 29 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed slightly firmer against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, and dealers said the local unit was aided by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cautiousness following weeks of Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- which had been selling yuan for dollars in a bid to slow the advance of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  until recently -- had turned more cautious due to the weakness of Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on international markets. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at its intraday high of 8.2900 to the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Tuesday from Monday's 8.2902. \par \par \uc2  "After the sharp depreciation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Southeast Asia, the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan to ensure there is no opportunity for speculators to force the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now wants to keep the yuan moving in a narrow range to avoid risks brought by speculative buying," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Speculators have only a limited chance to push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around as the unit is not fully convertible. China also has a large supply of dollars due to its trade surplus and an influx of investment capital. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2903. The yuan opened unchanged at 8.2902 and moved in a range of 8.2902/8.2905 for most of the session, touching an intraday low of 8.2908 before the close. Trading was more active than on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Buying of the yuan pushed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to test the key resistance level of 8.2900 again," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The rise was capped by selling at the 8.2900 level most probably from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan should breach the 8.2900 level on Wednesday. The yuan ended higher at 7.0526 from 7.0799 against 100 Japanese yen and at 1.0700 from 1.0702 to the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7t01wsw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
