\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up at two-year high vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 27 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed up at an intraday and two-year high of 8.2913 against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Tuesday, from Monday's 8.2930, with buying active below the key 8.2920 level, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The close was the highest since May 18, 1995 when the yuan ended at 8.2892. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2918 yuan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said buying in the yuan was active again on Monday after consolidating for the past few days. \par \par \uc2  A firm close above the key 8.2920 level indicated pro-yuan sentiment was strong on the market, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened higher at 8.2918 and fell slightly to hit an intraday low of 8.2922 early in trading before moving just above the 8.2920 level for most of the session. Trading was active with most business done at 8.2916, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Active buying was seen whenever the yuan moved below the 8.2920 level," one dealer said. "This supported the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and made it close firmly above that level." \par \par \uc2  A second dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , did little to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan as it has often done in the past. \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not act to depress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan is likely to breach the 8.2900 resistance level in the short term," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to continue to rise slightly on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed little changed at an intraday low of 7.1438 from 7.1501 against 100 Japanese yen and up slightly at 1.0718 from 1.0720 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5r04w6l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
