\par\par \b \uc2  FORECAST-Chinese yuan seen under pressure to rise. [CORRECTED 21:44 GMT] \b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1997\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 20 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan is under pressure to rise in the coming month due to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's high foreign trade surplus, but expected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep the uptrend under control, analysts said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to move mainly in a range between 8.2940 and 8.2930, against a range of 8.2950 to 8.2960 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade system, an interbank market, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan edged up to close at a seven-week high of 8.2949 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "China's high foreign trade surplus is likely to push more dollars on to the market, adding to the current oversupply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan is under heavy pressure to rise," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Despite an oversupply of dollars on the market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep firm control over the rising momentum of the Chinese yuan," said another trader. \par \par \uc2  China has announced that its foreign trade surplus was $6.71 billion in the first three months of 1997, against a deficit of $1.1 billion (corrects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from yuan) in the same 1996 period. \par \par \uc2  China's total 1996 foreign trade surplus was $12 billion, official figures show. Analysts said they expected the 1997 surplus to be much higher. \par \par \uc2  The official Business Daily said in a recent report the yuan was likely to continue to rise in 1997 after three years of consecutive rises due to the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and foreign trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  "In 1997, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply will continue to exceed demand, as it has for the past three years," the newspaper quoted an unidentified official with the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  as saying. \par \par \uc2  "The Chinese yuan will face pressure to rise further this year despite three consecutive years of rises," he said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan rose 0.3 percent in 1996 after a rise of 2.9 percent in 1994 and 1.5 percent in 1995. \par \par \uc2  By the end of February, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves hit a record high of $111 billion yuan, against $105 billion by the end of 1996 and $31.5 billion by the end of 1995, official figures show. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said other factors exerting upward pressure on the yuan include the continued flow of foreign investment into China. \par \par \uc2  Despite the yuan's rises, the People's Bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has consistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the yuan from surging, market sources said. \par \par \uc2  "This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been the major reason for the yuan to move mainly in that narrow range of 8.2950/8.5960 in the past month," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a seperate trading room on the market which enables it to access all trading details. \par \par \uc2  Other institutions trading on the market can only see details of their own transactions and so remain in the dark about other trades. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4k06sha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
