\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends little changed vs US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 9 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed at 8.2965 against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday from Tuesday's 8.2963 due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Tuesday was 8.2966. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened almost unchanged at 8.2965 and hardly moved in early trading. \par \par \uc2  It then fluctuated in a wider range, hitting an intraday high of 8.2909 and a low of 8.3016 mid-session before stabilising again around 8.2965 towards the close. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than on Tuesday with most business done at about 8.2965, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said significant buying by a Chinese bank around the mid-session made the yuan fluctuate widely for a period. They declined to name the bank. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring the yuan's movements back into a narrow range, they said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the yuan from rising in late trading," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some designated banks followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead in selling yuan. \par \par \uc2  Despite Wednesday's wide movements, traders said they expected the yuan to move in a narrow range over the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is likely to move around the 8.2970 level on Thursday, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 6.5700 from 6.6000 against 100 Japanese yen and higher at 1.0700 from 1.0713 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4907kcu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
