\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan seen holding current level. \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 03:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 24 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan is likely to stay at the current 8.2950-8.3000 level against the U.S. dollar for the next month on China's national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market based in Shanghai, analysts said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  There is a surplus of dollars on the market, the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, but this is likely to be offset by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's determination to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The Chinese yuan will move in a narrow range around the current level of 8.2950-8.3000 in the next month," a market trader said. "Market fundamentals will not change much and there is no market-moving news around the corner." \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed on Friday at 8.2960 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The key factor on the market is a surplus of dollars, which is not likely to change in the short term," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst. "But this over-supply will be neutralised by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the over-supply was mainly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign trade surplus, which hit $3.8 billion for the first two months of 1997 and which the analyst sources said could reach $4.6 billion by the end of March. \par \par \uc2  China expects a smooth flow of foreign investment this year, and some officials have estimated it will reach $49 billion, up by about 15 percent from 1996's $42.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  More dollars will be pumped into the Chinese market this month when the local branches of some foreign banks start to do local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  business. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given approval to eight overseas banks to do yuan business on certain pre-conditions which include moving their offices to Pudong, Shanghai's premier economic development zone across the Huangpu River from the city centre. \par \par \uc2  Of the eight, three -- Citibank of the United States, the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd and the Hong Kong & Shanghai Banking Corp -- have already moved to Pudong. \par \par \uc2  "In our local business, funding is expected to be a key problem," said a banker with one of the approved eight. \par \par \uc2  "We are very likely to resort to the interbank market as one means of yuan funding," he told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The start of yuan business by foreign banks is likely to add foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply on the interbank in the short term," said a second interbank market trader. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not likely to loosen control over the exchange rate on the market. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves hit a record high of $110 billion in February. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  felt reserves of $150 billion would be appropriate for China. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable this year and that policy will not change any time soon," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is expected to continue to buy dollars on the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was established in Shanghai in April 1994 and is tightly controlled. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an independent trading room on the market, through which it can monitor all transactions and make decisions accordingly. \par \par \uc2  Other members, in contrast, do not have access to any but their own trades and are thus kept in the dark about general market trends. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3o08bj5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
