\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes slightly down vs US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 17 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed slightly down at 8.2926 against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Monday from 8.2922 last Friday with no impact seen from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement that it intends to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2925. \par \par \uc2  The Beijing-based Financial Times newspaper last Friday quoted Zhou Xiaochuan, vice-governor of the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the yuan from rising sharply. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said his comments had no impact on market sentiment and the yuan moved stably in a narrow range between 8.2920 and 8.2930. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened little changed at 8.2923 and consolidated around 8.2920 for most of the session, hitting an intra-day high of 8.2918 and a low of 8.2927. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most done at 8.2922, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said Zhou's comments implied the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would depress the yuan if it rose too high. \par \par \uc2  "Given the yuan's already high level, and the active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, most people think the yuan has only limited upward potential in the short term," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move below the 8.2920 level on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed almost unchanged at 6.6460 from 6.6500 against 100 Japanese yen and little changed at an intra-day low of 1.0706 from 1.0705 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2h007sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
