\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends at 20-month high vs dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 5 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed up at a 20-month high of 8.2924 on Wednesday from Tuesday's 8.2932 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rise was mainly due to reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had sold the yuan heavily in early in the week to prevent it from rising sharply. \par \par \uc2  The rate toppled the former high of 8.2892 set on May 18, 1995. Trading was slow due the approach of the Chinese lunar new year holiday which begins on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened higher at 8.2926 and hit an intraday low of 8.2927 early in the session. It then rose steadily to move in a range of 8.2920 and 8.2924 for most of the session, hitting a high of 8.2900. \par \par \uc2  Most transactions were done at 8.2922, traders said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said bidding on the yuan was heavy with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reducing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but thin volume kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rising momentum to a minimum. \par \par \uc2  A second dealer said trading would be even slower on Thursday, the last trading day before the holiday. \par \par \uc2  "Tomorrow's transactions will be settled after the holiday according the exchange's T+1 settlement system," he said. "This will keep most traders from trading on Thursday." \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the yuan to remain stable in the range of 8.2920 and 8.2930 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 6.7500 from 6.8000 against 100 Japanese yen and down at an intraday low of 1.0700 from 1.0688 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt250313q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
