\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends up slightly against dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 4 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed up slightly on Tuesday at 8.2932, from Monday's 8.2935 against the U.S. dollar on Shanghai's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few minutes before closing to prevent the yuan from rising sharply, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at 8.2933 and remained stable around 8.2930 early in the session, touching an intraday low of 8.2935. It then rose steadily and hit a high of 8.2909 in late trading before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than on Monday with most transactions done at 8.2928, traders said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  depressed the yuan's uptrend and weakened strong pro-yuan sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reminds us of a similar move at the same time last year when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made use of thin trading during the holiday to force the yuan down," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market is largely dominated by a holiday mood, with the lunar new year holiday beginning on February 7, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A second dealer said that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to invervene in the market, the yuan's upward trend of the past few months could come to an end. \par \par \uc2  He said he expected the yuan to move around the 8.2930 level on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 6.8000 from 6.8270 against 100 Japanese yen and up slightly at an intraday high of 1.0688 from 1.0693 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2402yrt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
