\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes up against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 1 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed up at 8.2985 against the U.S. dollar on Friday from Thursday's 8.2999 on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with lower \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen reducing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the yuan at about 8.30, which made the yuan remain on its uptrend. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened little changed at 8.2998 and hit an intra-day low of 8.3000 early in the session. It then rose to move between 8.2980 and 8.2985 for the rest of the session, reaching a high of 8.2975. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active, with most done at about 8.2980, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Little selling emerged around the key 8.3000 resistance level which was breached yesterday," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually sells the yuan to prevent its rise, which it thinks is an effective way of controlling inflation," said a second dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Less active selling indicates that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was weaker," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the yuan to try to stand above 8.30 early next week. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up slightly at 7.2843 from 7.2995 against 100 Japanese yen and up at an intra-day high of 1.0723 from 1.0740 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \pa