\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes up at year-high against US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 20 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed up at a year-high for the fifth straight day on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, ending at 8.3026 on Friday from Thursday's 8.3036 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  They said that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's improving international trade balance and less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had boosted positive expectations of the yuan's trend. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at an intra-day low of 8.3035 and consolidated around 8.3030 for most of the session, hitting a high of 8.3020. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than yesterday, with most done at 8.3030, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan's continuous rises strengthened the confidence of buyers," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  less to depress the yuan, which has helped its uptrend over the past week," a second dealer said. "A rebound in the inflation rate limited the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's selling of the local unit." \par \par \uc2  China's retail inflation rate in August increased 1.5 percentage points from July to 8.1 percent, the first upturn since February. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the yuan to continue to rise early next week. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended slightly up at 7.5755 from 7.5805 against 100 Japanese yen, and down at an intra-day low of 1.0750 from 1.0745 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument l