\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes at year-high vs US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, September 16 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan ended up against the U.S. dollar on Monday in Shanghai at its highest closing level since August 14 last year due to strong pro-yuan sentiment sparked by China's growing foreign trade surplus, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended up at 8.3048 from last Friday's 8.3052 against the dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The previous higher closing rate of 8.3035 was set on August 14 last year. \par \par \uc2  Local media reported on Saturday that China posted a trade surplus of $2.99 billion in August, bringing the surplus in the first eight months of this year to $4.99 billion. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the news prompted strong bids for the yuan today and pushed it to close above the main 8.3050 resistance level. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan breached the main resistance level today after weeks of consolidation due to the news of the trade surplus," said one trader. "Many traders expect the yuan to continue to rise due to a surplus of the dollar on the market, with China's foreign trade position growing stronger." \par \par \uc2  "The yuan is widely expected to continue rising in the short term," a second dealer said. "But it is likely to go up slowly because of expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan since the market was established in 1994, to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In today's trading, the yuan opened slightly up at 8.3051. \par \par \uc2  After hitting an intra-day low of 8.3053 early in the session, it rose above the 8.3050 level and consolidated in a range of 8.3046-8.3048 for most of the session. \par \par \uc2  It hit a high of 8.3040 about 15 minutes before closing. \par \par \uc2  Trading was more active than last Friday, with most done at about 8.3047, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan would move around 8.3050 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at an intra-day high of 7.5030 from 7.5250 against 100 Japanese yen and also at an intra-day high of 1.0732, up from 1.0737 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9g033eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
