\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends unchanged against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, September 12 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed unchanged at 8.3053 against the U.S dollar on Thursday on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan hit a high of 8.3041 in intra-day trading, the highest level in the past year, due to strong pro-yuan sentiment but failed to close high due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan this week," said a trader. "Had there been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan would have risen sharply due to strong pro-yuan sentiment." \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at 8.3051 today and moved around 8.3052 for most of the session, hitting an intra-day low of 8.3065 twice and a high of 8.3041 in late trading. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull, with most done at about 8.3052. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the yuan to consolidate around the 8.3050 level on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 7.5241 from 7.5480 against 100 Japanese yen and unchanged at an intra-day low of 1.0750 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9c037qj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
