\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends slightly up vs US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, September 11 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed slightly up at 8.3053 on Wednesday from Tuesday's 8.3055 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market due to strong pro-yuan sentiment, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan rose despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to depress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around the key 8.3050 resistance level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at 8.3055 and consolidated around its opening price for most of the session, hitting an intra-day high of 8.3050 and a low of 8.3057 in mid-session. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull, with most done at about 8.3054. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yuan hit the 8.3050 level," said one trader. "It sold the yuan to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prevent it from rising sharply." \par \par \uc2  "Selling of the yuan by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has prevented it from rising sharply for three successive days," said a second trader. "As a result, it seems difficult for the yuan to rise much this week." \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the yuan to move around 8.3050 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended up at 7.5480 from 7.5850 against 100 Japanese yen on the yen's weakness on the world market. It closed down at an intra-day low of 1.0750 from 1.0735 against the H.K. dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds