\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends up at year-high against US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, August 14 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan ended at a year-high of 8.3076 on Wednesday, slightly up from Tuesday's 8.3080, against the U.S dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at 8.3076, hitting an intraday low of 8.3078 early in the session. It consolidated in a wide range for the rest of the session, hitting a intraday high of 8.3058 15 minutes before closing. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active and most was done at 8.3070, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said buying was stronger than in the past few days but rises were capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Bids, possibly from the head office of a bank in Beijing, pushed the yuan up to 8.3060 late in the session." said one dealer. "But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped the uptrend." \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the yuan to move up toward 8.3070 in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 7.6920 from 7.7000 against 100 Japanese yen and slightly up at 1.0730 from 1.0733 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8e049hj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
