\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan sets year-high closing price vs U.S. dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 12 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed up at 8.3086 on Monday from Friday's 8.3090 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, its highest closing level since August 17, 1995. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan moved steadily up today but its rise was capped at 8.3080 by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at 8.3090 and consolidated in a range of 8.3085-8.3087 for most of the session, hitting an intra-day high of 8.3081 and low of 8.3093. Trading was dull. \par \par \uc2  "Only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could slow its rise," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the yuan to close above the 8.3080 level on Tuesday despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to strong pro-yuan sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 7.6888 from 7.6700 against 100 Japanese yen and slightly up at 1.0735 from 1.0740 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8c04evi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
