\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan to move slightly up in rest of 1996. \b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1996\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 2 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan is expected to inch up against the U.S. dollar for the rest of 1996 after a strong uptrend in the past few weeks, analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The determination of the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from fluctuating sharply and a worsening foreign trade performance will offset an oversupply of dollars in the market, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has risen for the past three weeks and repeatedly hit five-month highs on the Shanghai-based China interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It closed at 8.3104 against the dollar on Friday, up about 0.30 percent from three weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the yuan to continue rising in the short term but think it is unlikely to overcome key resistance at the 8.3000 level by the end of this year. \par \par \uc2  "This year foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply has far exceeded demand on the market and nationwide, as reflected by surging \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves this year," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  The reserves hit a record $86.6 billion at the end of June, up from $73.5 billion at end-1995, official figures show. \par \par \uc2  One main source of incoming capital was direct foreign investment which reached $19.6 billion in the first half of 1996, up 20 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  "China's foreign trade position is weakening this year, with exports dropping sharply, limiting the inflow of dollars," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  "But this is partly compensated by other sources including surging foreign investment, making the dollar oversupply likely to continue for the rest of the year," he said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yuan's recent uptrend was also due to a technical rebound after falls in the first five months of this year on rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would devaluate the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . An official later denied the speculation. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmly capped the yuan's upward trend despite strong pro-yuan sentiment on the market," said a second trader. "Had it not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan would have surged in the past few weeks." \par \par \uc2  "With Beijing preparing for renminbi convertibility under the current account by year-end, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not allow the yuan to fluctuate too sharply," he added. \par \par \uc2  The current account convertibility was promised by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong last month. \par \par \uc2  Bearish for the yuan is the performance of exports, which are expected to fall sharply this year after surges in the past few years, official media has said. \par \par \uc2  "The fall in exports will reduce the inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , preventing the yuan from rising sharply late this year," said a Shanghai-based banker with the Bank of China. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8204mg3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
