\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  yuan up on trade surplus, less  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 1996\par 11:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 26 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan has hit a five-month closing high against the U.S. dollar five times in the past 10 days because of an improved trade outlook and less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.3115 to the dollar on Friday, up from a low of 8.3365 three months ago. \par \par \uc2  "The increase in exports is the main reason for the yuan's rises in the last few days," a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  China posted a foreign trade surplus of $880 million in the first half of 1996, after a deficit of $490 million in the first five months. \par \par \uc2  "Supply of U.S. dollars exceeds demand on the market, with most banks selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because foreign-funded firms are selling them large quantities of U.S. dollars," an analyst said. \par \par \uc2  "The new settlement system of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for foreign-funded firms starting from July 1 caused banks to have excessive U.S. dollars to sell," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Since July 1, foreign-funded companies in China have been allowed to trade foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through designated banks. \par \par \uc2  In addition, a ceiling volume was set for their holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They are required to sell excess amounts to the banks in exchange for renminbi. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investment to China has continued to rise, which also helped to strengthen pro-yuan sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "The rise of foreign investment makes China have more U.S. dollars, resulting in over-supply of the U.S. dollar on the market," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  China has attracted direct foreign investment of $19.6 billionin the first half of this year, up 20 percent compared with the same period last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Securities newspaper reported on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan had eased in the past few days, which has encouraged yuan buying on the market. \par \par \uc2  An official of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said early this year that the bank would not devalue the yuan to encourage exports. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan has really dropped," said a local analyst. "Actually, it hasn't acted to depress the yuan in the past few weeks, it has just curbed the rate of the yuan's rise to stabilise the market." \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts said the yuan was likely to rise further for the rest of the session, but its upside would still be capped within the 8.30 range with the government determined to maintain astable exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan will rise further in the second half of this year, but is unlikely to move up sharply, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will limit it," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7q04xm8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
