\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends at five-month high vs dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 26 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan ended at a five-month closing high of 8.3115 on Friday, its fifth successive such high, up from Thursday's 8.3128 against the U.S dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said pro-yuan sentiment continued to dominate the market after China posted a foreign trade surplus of $880 million in the first half of 1996. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan today but only to a limited extent, they said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, which has helped the yuan go up, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at an intra-day low of 8.3127 today and moved up to consolidate in a narrow range of 8.3210 and 8.3215 for most of the session, hitting a high of 8.3108. Trading was active, with most done at about 8.3115. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the yuan to continue to rise early next week, testing the 8.3100 resistance level. But room for further rises will be limited after sharp gains in the past few weeks. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 7.6701 from 7.6150 against 100 Japanese yen on Monday and down at 1.0758 from 1.0750 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  --Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7q04xb7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
