\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan up on foreign firm export rises. \b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1996\par 13:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 10 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan has continued to rise against the U.S. dollar in the past three months, helped largely by a surge in exports by foreign-funded firms in China in the first half of the year, dealers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The export value of foreign-funded firms was $6.33 billion in the first four months, up 40.7 percent year-on-year and the growth is expected to continue for the rest of this year, the China-based International Finance News said this week. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 8.3164 on Wednesday, up from a low of 8.3365 three months ago. It has set a new four-month high on each of the past three days on strong pro-yuan market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "Supply of the U.S. dollar exceeds its demand on the market with most banks selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because foreign-funded firms are selling large quantities of U.S. dollars to them," an analyst said. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign-funded firms did well in terms of exports in the first half of this year, which gave them more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We have been buying more U.S. dollars from foreign-funded enterprises than we have been selling in the first half of the year, so we are selling excessive foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market," said a dealer with a domestic commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was also a factor for the recent rise in the renminbi. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the biggest buyer of U.S. dollars on the market, but it has not capped the yuan's rises over the past three days," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said trading on the market was slow despite continued rises, with foreign-funded firms now selling their excess foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to banks instead of authorising banks to trade the funds on the market. \par \par \uc2  Since July 1, foreign-funded companies in China are allowed to trade foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through designated banks. \par \par \uc2  In addition, a ceiling has been set for their holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They are required to sell excess amounts to the banks. \par \par \uc2  "Banks can digest most of the excess foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from foreign-funded firms, which has made trading volume on the market fall," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the reduction in trading volume was hard to reverse and they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange to consider providing new trading instruments to re-activate the market. \par \par \uc2  "The new policy on settlements has affected the trading volume, and if no new instruments are introduced, it will be difficult to turn it round," said an analyst. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange is likely to revive the trading of three-month foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts, which was once tried but later deleted," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  An official from the exchange said they were studying the possibility of introducing new instruments but declined to give further details. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7a05n3x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
