\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends down against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 4 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed down slightly at 8.3202 on Thursday from Wednesday's 8.3200 against the U.S dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to depress the yuan at the 8.3202 level to cap its uptrend after three days of rises, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly lower at 8.3202 and consolidated in a narrow range of 8.3200 and 8.3202 for most of the session, hitting an intra-day low of 8.3211 at the mid-session and a high of 8.3188 several minutes before closing. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most done around 8.3202. \par \par \uc2  Traders said buying pushed the yuan above the main resistance level at 8.3200 during the trading, but it could not stand firm due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want the yuan to rise sharply," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the yuan to continue to move in a narrow range around the 8.3200 level on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended up at 7.5500 from 7.5700 against 100 Japanese yen and up at 1.0737 from 1.0763 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7405xse\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
