\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes up against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 27 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed up at 8.3216 on Thursday from Wednesday's 8.3226 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on a technical rebound after two days of falls, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened higher at an intra-day low of 8.3218 and rose to hit a high of 8.3198 early in the session before falling back and moving mainly in a narrow range of 8.3210 and 8.3216. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active with most done at about 8.3210. \par \par \uc2  Traders said despite today's rebound, pro-yuan sentiment was weakening gradually after the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan over the past two days. \par \par \uc2  "This made the yuan fail to close above the 8.3200 resistance level today," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The Shanghai Securities News said today that Beijing would supply huge new working capital loans to 300 key state firms in the second half of this year to support their development. \par \par \uc2  "The news depressed market sentiment today," a second trader said. "Such a move indicates that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is partially loosening the tight monetary policy adopted since mid-1993 which is likely to weaken the yuan's trend in the short term." \par \par \uc2  But traders said on Friday, the yuan was likely to consolidate around the 8.3220 level. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed slightly down at 7.6020 from 7.6000 against 100 Japanese yen and unchanged at 1.0760 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Li