\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes down against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 17 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed down at 8.3226 on Monday from last Friday's 8.3211 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened little changed at 8.3210 and quickly moved up to a three-month high of 8.3195 early in the session, breaching a key support at the 8.3200 level. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was then seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars, forcing the yuan to fall and consolidate in a range of 8.3220 and 8.3228, traders said. It hit an intra-day low of 8.3230 in late trading, they said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull early on but active for the rest of the time, with most done at about 8.3220, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yuan broke through the main resistance level of 8.3200. \par \par \uc2  "Some designated banks also sold the yuan along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helping push it down," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  A second trader said today's trend showed that 8.3200 would remain a major resistance level in the short term. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yuan would move around 8.3220 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan fell to 7.6200 from 7.6151 against 100 Japanese yen and to 1.0760 from 1.0739 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds6h0