\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes down against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 7 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed down at 8.3237 on Friday from Thursday's 8.3230 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The fall ended the yuan's rise of the past three trading days but it still hit a new three-month high of 8.3221 in intra-day trading today, indicating pro-yuan sentiment is still strong, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened lower at 8.3235 and hit an intra-day high of 8.3221 early in the session. It then fell to move mostly between 8.3235 and 8.3240, hitting a low of 8.3244 in late trading. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull, with most down at about 8.3237. \par \par \uc2  Tradera said that, when the yuan reached the new three-month high, the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  depressed the yuan to keep it stable," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 7.6300 from 7.5920 against 100 Japanese yen and down at 1.0759 from 1.0740 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai newsroom (86-21) 6279-7004 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds670719w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
