\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends unchanged against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 20 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed unchanged at 8.3280 against the U.S. dollar on Monday on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly lower at 8.3283 and moved in a narrow box of 8.3280-8.3285 for most of the session, hitting an intra-day low of 8.3293 and a high of 8.3278 around the mid-session. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active with most done at about 8.3280. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yuan managed to stand firmly above 8.3300 after breaking the resistance level last Friday, partly due to less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have no intention to push the yuan below the 8.3300 yuan level," one trader said. "This helped the yuan keep steady today." \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was a pro-yuan sentiment on the market today and thay expected the yuan to continue a strong run in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 7.7230 from 7.8090 against 100 Japanese yen and unchanged at 1.0760 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds5k07oit\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
