\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends unchanged against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 8 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed unchanged at 8.3302 on Wednesday against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at 8.3301 and moved around the 8.3300 level for most of the session, hitting an intra-day high of 8.3288 and a low of 8.3305 late in the session. Trading was dull with most done at about 8.3300, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said buying in the yuan was strong today but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to close above the 8.3300 resistance level due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "A southern bank bought the yuan continuously in today's trading and pushed it above 8.3300 for some time," said one trader. "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it below the level at the close." \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been moving around 8.3300 for about three weeks. One trader said the market had lost direction without fresh market-moving news. Traders said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stay close to current levels over the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 7.8950 against 100 Japanese yen from Tuesday's 7.9075 and ended down at an intra-day low of 1.0783 from 1.0773 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds5808bjh\par }\page 