\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends down against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 17 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed down at an intra-day low of 8.3330 on Wednesday from Tuesday's 8.3315 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly up at 8.3312 and moved upward steadily for most of the session, hitting an intra-day high of 8.3301 late in the session before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it close at the day's low, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active, with most done at about 8.3314, traders said. Volumes are not posted on the market. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected." said a trader. "The bank does not want to see the yuan rise above the key resistance at 8.3300." \par \par \uc2  One trader said the yuan rose early in the session on buying by other banks, possibly the Bank of China. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the yuan to rise on Thursday to around the 8.3320 level. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 7.6661 from 7.6425 against 100 Japanese yen and almost unchanged at 1.0760 from 1.0761 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4h096ak\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
