\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends at ten-month low on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 22 (Reuter) - The yuan closed at a ten-month low against the U.S. dollar on Friday on \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, mainly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It closed at an intra-day low of 8.3365, down from Thursday's 8.3320. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at 8.3320 and consolidated around that level early in the session, hitting a high of 8.3309. \par \par \uc2  It then fell and moved mainly around the 8.3350 level before closing at the intra-day low. Trading was active, with most deals done at 8.3350. \par \par \uc2  "Although the yuan was stable around the 8.3320 level in early trading today, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it sharply down at the close," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Traders said designated banks followed the example of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold the yuan late in the session. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a stronger dollar on the world market also helped push the yuan down. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up at 7.7401 from 7.8300 vs 100 Japanese yen and up at 1.0760 from 1.0788 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds3m001l7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
