\par\par \b \uc2  China/Taiwan-2: Taiwan Govt Spending To Stabilize Markets \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 01:09\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    On Friday, Beijing announced a third round of military\par exercises that will wrap around Taiwan-controlled islands\par near China. On Saturday, a Foreign Ministry spokesman\par reiterated China's long-held position that it won't\par renounce the use of force to recover Taiwan.\par    At the same time, though, Beijing sent the clearest\par signals yet that it isn't intent on hurting Taiwan's\par economy, with official news accounts explicitly separating\par economic and political interests in the cross-straits\par relationship.\par    "It is our sincere hope that the people of Taiwan can\par live their lives in peace and stability. I don't think it\par is difficult to achieve," Chinese Premier Li Peng said\par Sunday.\par    Saying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wouldn't brook military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par outside forces - a thinly disguised warning to U.S.\par warships that have gathered to monitor China's exercises -\par Li appeared even to accept the prospect of Lee Teng-hui's\par near-certain victory this weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "What is most important is that the leader of Taiwan,\par no matter how he is selected, refrain from carrying out\par actions aimed at creating `two Chinas' or leading to\par independence for Taiwan in the future," he said. Those\par comments may help to soothe the markets.\par    Since the beginning of the month, the government and\par leading banks and insurance companies have thrown close to\par $1 billion a week at the market - down 13% since last June\par - accounting for up to one-third of daily trading volume.\par    The government has pledged another $11 billion if\par tensions persist, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has spent heavily\par to stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 03-17-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1909EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4080 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013ds3i00nb2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
