\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan closes sharply down vs US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 15 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed sharply down on Thursday at an intra-day low of 8.3139 from 8.3104 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market mainly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at an intra-day high of 8.3104 and fell, consolidating mostly in a range of 8.3115-8.3120 early in the session when the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling yuan, they said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active, with most transactions done at about 8.3118, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action was taken early in the session and aimed to reverse the yuan's firm trend in the past few trading days," said one trader. "There was also follow-up yuan selling that forced it to close lower." \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expect the yuan to go up slightly to move around the 8.3120 level for the rest of this week. \par \par \uc2  The exchange has decided to continue trading on Saturday and Sunday to compensate for closing on Thursday and Friday next week during the Lunar New Year holiday, officials said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 7.8200 from 7.7611 vs 100 Japanese yen and down at 1.0760 from 1.0740 vs the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2f01i7l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
