\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends down against US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 3 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed down at 8.3200 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, losing 20 points from Monday's 8.3180, mainly due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened slightly higher at 8.3177 and moved around 8.3175 early in the session, hitting an intra-day high of 8.3171. It quickly fell to a low of 8.3210 at mid-session before rebounding to consolidate at around the 8.3200 level. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active with most done at 8.3197 and 8.3176. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the fall today was mainly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was also some dollar bidding from other parties after the yuan began to drop at the mid-session," said one dealer. He declined to specify the dollar buyers. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the trend in the past two days indicated there might be a slight uptrend for the dollar in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended up at an intra-day high of 7.9800 from 8.0100 against 100 Japanese yen and was unchanged at 1.0763 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds1303bsg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
