\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends down against U.S. dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 7 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan moved down against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based interbank market, with the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.3143, from 8.3133 on Wednesday. It opened flat at 8.3133 and quickly moved to hit an intra-day high of 8.3123 before falling back, hitting a low of 8.3145. Most trading was done at 8.3135, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan was in a consolidation phase today," said one trader. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  depressed the yuan steadily in the second half when trading was thin." \par \par \uc2  Some dealers speculated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aim in pushing the yuan down against the dollar was to give exporters the benefit of greater \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains on the balance sheets. \par \par \uc2  They said the yuan's trend on Friday was likely to be indicative of its movement for the rest of the month. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 8.1946 from 8.1905 against 100 Japanese yen and was little changed at 1.0754 from 1.0753 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drc700vm5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
