\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese yuan closes at record high for eighth day. \b0\par\par\uc2 226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 4 (Reuter) - The Chinese yuan closed at a record high, 8.3580 against the U.S. dollar, for the eighth consecutive day on the Shanghai-based interbank market. \par \par \uc2  This jump of 204 points from Wednesday's close of 8.3784 the was the second largest intra-day gain since the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade Centre opened in April last year. The largest jump, 254 points, was on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan also hit a record intra-day higg, of 8.3557, on Thursday. Floor sources said there was heavy selling in dollars and that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had done little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been rising against the dollar since the establishment of the market. However, its upwards momentum was much strengthened at the start of last week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they believed the bank was now aiming for a more market-driven yuan-dollar rate. "We have become accustomed to the rapid appreciation of the yuan as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying less and less," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended higher at 1.0813 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0833 on Wednesday. It fell to 10.0109 against 100 Japanese yen, from 9.9065. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr540830h\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdr